 04:44 results -> ../investigation\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 05:43 scientific-evidence\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 05:28 scripts\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 05:18 source_evidence\n-rw-------  1 agent agent     265 Nov  7 04:59 strategy_validation_feedback.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent     271 Nov  7 04:59 strategy_validation_feedback.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 agent agent    4096 Nov  7 05:03 tables\nlrwxrwxrwx  1 agent agent       7 Nov  7 04:44 task -> ../task\n-rw-------  1 agent agent    2909 Nov  7 05:43 validation_feedback.json\n-rw-------  1 agent agent    2090 Nov  7 05:43 validation_feedback.md\n-rw-------  1 agent agent   22864 Nov  7 05:43 validation_report.json\n\n--- VENUE.md ---\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\n\n--- validation_feedback.json ---\n{\n  \"agentic_evidence_audit\": {\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"finding_count\": 0,\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"summary\": \"Main and supplementary claims match the final evaluation, grounding artifacts, and evidence trail; qualification, validity, source-identity, and missing-ablation limitations remain explicit.\",\n    \"verdict\": \"pass\"\n  },\n  \"evidence_validation\": {\n    \"bundle_path\": \"work/results/t10/codex/20261107_014149/paper/scientific-evidence\",\n    \"bundle_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"dangling\": [],\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"paper_token_count\": 116,\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"anchored_references\": 69,\n      \"dangling_references\": 0,\n      \"manifests_checked\": 14,\n      \"resolved_references\": 47,\n      \"total_references\": 116\n    },\n    \"verification_report_path\": \"work/results/t10/codex/20261107_014149/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json\"\n  },\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-07T05:43:16.029366+00:00\",\n  \"hard_errors\": [\n    \"figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for coverage_width_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for rare_outcome_diagnostic\"\n  ],\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"page_validation\": {\n    \"body_pages\": null,\n    \"checked\": false,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"exclude_references\": false,\n    \"last_body_page_counted\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_number\": null,\n    \"max_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"paper_format\": null,\n    \"reference_start_page\": null,\n    \"supplement_pages\": 0,\n    \"supplement_start_page\": null,\n    \"total_pages\": null\n  },\n  \"paper_dir\": \"work/results/t10/codex/20261107_014149/paper\",\n  \"pdf_path\": null,\n  \"soft_warnings\": [\n    \"figures[0].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\",\n    \"figures[0] PNG height too small: 630 < 700\",\n    \"figures[1].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\",\n    \"figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\",\n    \"figures[2].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\",\n    \"figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\",\n    \"figures[2] PNG height too small: 690 < 700\"\n  ],\n  \"supplementary_information_validation\": {\n    \"appendix_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"heading_present\": true,\n    \"placed_after_references\": true,\n    \"pre_bibliography_clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"rendered_checked\": false,\n    \"rendered_heading_present\": false,\n    \"rendered_visible_character_count\": 0,\n    \"substantive_element_count\": 5,\n    \"visible_character_count\": 14699\n  }\n}\n--- validation_feedback.md ---\n# Paper validation feedback\n\n- generated_at: 2026-11-07T05:43:16.029366+00:00\n- paper_dir: `work/results/t10/codex/20261107_014149/paper`\n- ok: `False`\n\n## Hard errors\n- figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for coverage_width_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for rare_outcome_diagnostic\n\n## Supplementary Information validation\n- appendix_present: `True`\n- heading_present: `True`\n- placed_after_references: `True`\n- pre_bibliography_clearpage_present: `True`\n- clearpage_present: `True`\n- visible_character_count: `14699`\n- substantive_element_count: `5`\n- rendered_checked: `False`\n- rendered_heading_present: `False`\n- rendered_visible_character_count: `0`\n\n## Evidence validation\n- bundle_path: `work/results/t10/codex/20261107_014149/paper/scientific-evidence`\n- bundle_present: `True`\n- verification_report: `work/results/t10/codex/20261107_014149/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json`\n- total_references: `116`\n- resolved_references: `47`\n- anchored_references: `69`\n- dangling_references: `0`\n- manifests_checked: `14`\n\n## Agentic evidence audit\n- checked: `True`\n- verdict: `pass`\n- finding_count: `0`\n- summary: Main and supplementary claims match the final evaluation, grounding artifacts, and evidence trail; qualification, validity, source-identity, and missing-ablation limitations remain explicit.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[0].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\n- figures[0] PNG height too small: 630 < 700\n- figures[1].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[2].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[2] PNG height too small: 690 < 700\n\n--- draft_reference_gaps.md ---\n# Draft Reference Gap Analysis\n\n**Status:** `no_gaps`\n\nThe draft directly cites its comparator families and methodological foundations, and its remaining limitations require experimental or provenance evidence rather than targeted reference retrieval.\n\n## Scope and Checks\n\nReviewed `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, `references_provenance.json`, `claims_grounding.json`, `paper_data.json`, `paper_strategy.json`, and `global_memory_summary.md`. All 25 distinct manuscript citation keys resolve in both the bibliography and reference provenance. This consistency check supports, but does not by itself establish, the paragraph-level assessment below; recorded consultation scopes are not treated as full-text verification of every cited work.\n\n## Paragraph-Level Assessment\n\n- **Introduction:** The prediction-powered correction principle is directly attributed to `Angelopoulos2023PPI`. The frozen-input question is framed as this study's question, not an unsupported novelty or benchmark-superiority claim. Its empirical positioning is grounded in the recorded comparisons.\n- **Related Work — Prediction-assisted estimation:** PPI and PPI++ have direct citations (`Angelopoulos2023PPI`, `Angelopoulos2023PPIpp`). Control variates, survey calibration, model-assisted estimation, and missing-data context also have explicit references. No named comparator family in this paragraph lacks direct support.\n- **Related Work — Fitted controls and sample separation:** Semiparametric residualization, double/debiased learning, ridge regularization, GCV, cross-validation, and spline approximation are explicitly cited. The paragraph carefully limits the analogy to other fitted-nuisance methods rather than claiming their guarantees for the evaluated interval.\n- **Related Work — Intervals near the boundary:** Exact-binomial, score-based, adjusted, and Wald-coverage discussions already cite interval-comparison literature. Bounded-observation and empirical-Bernstein constructions also have direct foundations. Adding original historical interval citations would be optional attribution, not a material retrieval need for this paragraph.\n- **Method and Supplementary Information:** Source-level implementation choices are separately grounded, the fixed-control variance identity is derived, and fitted-control qualifications cite semiparametric references. The separate safety argument cites `MaurerPontil2009` and `Hoeffding1963`; it is not presented as measured evidence or a guarantee for the returned asymptotic interval.\n- **Experimental Protocol and Evidence Scope:** The paired-t approximation has a direct reference, multiplicity is explicitly acknowledged, and the manuscript does not claim simultaneous inference. Quantitative results and comparator endpoint descriptions come from the grounded records rather than requiring literature support.\n\n## Exclusions and Decision\n\nMissing condition generators, sample sizes, exact comparator versions, verified final source identity, and matched calibration or safety-track experiments cannot be supplied by citations. Broader literature expansion would not repair those limitations and is not necessary for the draft's condition-specific thesis. The strategy's earlier warning about absent PPI/PPI++ and interval/concentration foundations is superseded by their presence in the current manuscript, bibliography, and provenance.\n\n**Missing literatures:** None identified that justify targeted post-draft retrieval.\n\n**Rewrite targets:** None.\n\n**Failure reason:** None.\n\nNo reference retrieval was performed. `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, and `references_provenance.json` remain unchanged.\n\n--- draft_reference_gaps.json ---\n{\n  \"status\": \"no_gaps\",\n  \"summary\": \"The draft directly cites its comparator families and methodological foundations, and its remaining limitations require experimental or provenance evidence rather than targeted reference retrieval.\",\n  \"missing_literatures\": [],\n  \"rewrite_targets\": [],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
